A. closed forms (sympy)
   sigma*R = (sqrt(2*x + 1) - 1)/(4*pi)    p*R = (-x + sqrt(2*x + 1) - 1)/(8*pi*sqrt(2*x + 1))
  sigma*R, p*R are functions of x = m/R alone                            ok
  sigma*R == (sqrt(1+2x) - 1)/(4 pi)                                     ok
  p*R == (1 - (1+x)/sqrt(1+2x))/(8 pi)                                   ok
  (1+x)^2 - (1+2x) == x^2  (so p < 0 for every x > 0)                    ok
  8 pi sqrt(1+2x) (sigma+p) R == 1 + 3x - sqrt(1+2x)                     ok
  (1+3x)^2 - (1+2x) == 4x + 9x^2 > 0  (so sigma + p > 0 for every x > 0) ok
   |p|/sigma -> 0 (x->0),  -> 1/4 (x->oo)
  |p|/sigma -> 0 as x -> 0 and -> 1/4 as x -> oo                         ok
   |p|/sigma = x*(2 - 3*x)/8 + O(x^3)
  |p|/sigma < 1/4 at x = 1e-6 .. 1e8 (margin to DEC >= 3/4 sigma)        ok

